  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "atxJRUjARJLYZ/GKkir9tMoFFJ8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:28:45.920Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "ADR 0001 is marked **Status: Proposed** (2026-07-16, decider acaldas, \"Implements: TBD\"), so nothing in it describes current behaviour. What it describes is the problem and a design.\n\nThe problem: Connect eagerly syncs an entire drive on connect. Opening a remote drive on a Switchboard reactor streams the **full operation history of every document from timestamp 0** and replays it locally. Two costs follow \u2014 a cold load proportional to the whole drive regardless of what the user looks at, and **no prioritization**, so the document the user actually opened has no priority over the thousands they never touch.\n\nThe proposed design is lazy sync built on the sync protocol (explicitly *not* on the fetch/GraphQL document subgraphs, which would introduce a second divergent read path), opt-in, with minimal Connect changes: sync the drive document first because it lists its children, then sync a document's operations when it is opened; opening waits for that initial sync and is writable afterwards.\n\nTwo facts constrain any alternative and are worth remembering independently of the ADR. The **sync cursor is per-channel, collection-wide and forward-only**, so a live channel's filter cannot be widened to backfill a document whose operations predate the cursor. And a document's operation log is reachable **only through a collection it belongs to** \u2014 `operation-index.find` inner-joins on `document_collections`.\n\nThe ADR targets the legacy `powerhouse/document-drive` model, whose node list can diverge from `document_collections`.\n\n## Provenance\n- `docs/adr/0001-lazy-drive-sync.md` \u2014 Status header; Context; Decision (opening paragraphs)\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:28:45.920Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:28:45.920Z"
    }
  },
